       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**The problem:** Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended dose. The usual adult dose is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg/day is the maximum. A 50 mg dose could cause severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia, and dangerous swelling. Amlodipine has a long half-life (about 30\u201350 hours) and isn't removed by dialysis, so an overdose is hard to reverse.\n\nThis looks like it could be a typo for **5 mg**, which is a common starting dose.\n\n**What would you like to do?**\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** I can enter this right away if that's what you meant.\n2. **Another dose within 2.5\u201310 mg**, such as 10 mg.\n3. **50 mg as written.** If this is intentional, please confirm and give a clinical reason. I'll put it in the order note so pharmacy can see it during verification."
