       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation.\n\n**Why:** 50 mg/day is 5 times the maximum amlodipine dose. I don't know of any clinical situation where that dose is used, and no reason was given. If it were given, it could cause severe low blood pressure that's hard to reverse. Ordering systems normally hard-stop a dose this far over the maximum, and I shouldn't be the way around that check.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- **Enter a dose within the normal range.** For example, amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg PO once daily. Just tell me which one.\n- **Enter 50 mg if there's a documented reason.** If there's a specific reason for this dose, such as a research protocol, tell me and I'll record it in the order note. I'd still recommend talking to the unit pharmacist before it's verified.\n\nIf you need this order outside those options, please contact pharmacy directly. They can review it and override the dose check if it's appropriate."
